    {
      "id": "tr-inductors-3",
      "title": "Inductor challenges",
      "kind": "challenge",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "q1",
          "type": "numeric",
          "params": {
            "L1": [
              0.01,
              0.02,
              0.05
            ],
            "L2": [
              0.01,
              0.03,
              0.04
            ],
            "M": [
              0.002,
              0.005,
              0.008
            ]
          },
          "prompt": "Two coupled coils ($L_1$ = {{L1|H}}, $L_2$ = {{L2|H}}, $M$ = {{M|H}}) are connected in series so that the same current enters both dotted terminals. What is the total inductance of the series connection?",
          "answer": "L1+L2+2*M",
          "unit": "H",
          "explanation": "Both currents enter the dots, so the mutual terms are positive: $v_1 = (L_1 + M)\\,di/dt$ and $v_2 = (M + L_2)\\,di/dt$. Total: $v = (L_1 + L_2 + 2M)\\,di/dt$, so $L$ = {{L1|H}} + {{L2|H}} + 2 × {{M|H}} = {{L1+L2+2*M|H}}."
